				153,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Element submodule and add dependency repo transfer script\n\nThe Element submodule advances to ec552494 with purely mechanical formatting normalization across Air, Common, Echo, Grove, Mountain, Rest, and Vine — standardizing whitespace, import organization, dev_log! alignment, and lock patterns across 200+ files with no functional changes.\n\nAdd Maintain/Transfer/Dependency/Minor.sh to automate one-shot transfer of 16 dependency repositories (Biome, OXC, Rolldown, SWC, Vercel across Cargo/NPM/Dependency variants plus DocumentationLand) from CodeEditorLand to DependencyCodeEditorLand organization. Script supports dry-run mode, idempotent skip logic, and per-repo retry commands on failure.\n\nFormatting consistency maintained across Element components; new operational tooling for dependency repository governance.",
			"SHA": "5740d1fead3219c7f461f5b43739b74ee3f331d6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-07T17:06:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				151,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Element submodule to latest upstream revisions\n\nUpdate the Element submodule across all 13 components (Cocoon, Common, Echo, Grove, Maintain, Mist, Mountain, Output, Rest, SideCar, Sky, Vine, Wind) to synchronize with upstream revisions.\n\nMaintain applies consistent formatting and lint allowances, consolidating README emoji into component titles. Mountain standardizes whitespace and formatting across 150+ files in Air client integration, application state DTOs, environment providers, IPC command handlers, extension management, and Cocoon gRPC service handlers, and adds WorkingCopyDispatcher and WorkspaceDispatcher for WindServiceHandlers command routing. All other submodules advance with routine merge updates and mechanical formatting normalizations.\n\nAll changes maintain API compatibility with no functional modifications or breaking changes.",
			"SHA": "db20e7b176725d5d8fb15b37cdb5a0751527e458"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-07T17:00:02Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				151,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Dependency and Element submodules with README formatting normalization\n\nUpdate both submodule trees to synchronize with upstream formatting improvements and maintenance revisions.\n\nDependency submodule advances Biome, OXC, and Tauri nested submodules with README restructuring: Biome applies proper HTML indentation, self-closing tags, and em-space entities across seven repository entries; OXC corrects malformed showcase table markup with valid <picture>/<tr>/<td> structure; Tauri reformats PluginsWorkspace permission tables from flat to expanded multi-line layout and removes extraneous </rater> tags from TauriSearch test fixtures. All changes are presentational — preserving every link, badge, and semantic content.\n\nElement submodule batches updates across all 14 components (Air, Cocoon, Common, Echo, Grove, Maintain, Mist, Mountain, Output, Rest, SideCar, Sky, Vine, Worker). README header tables consolidated by merging emoji/icon cells into component names using Unicode em-space (&#x2001;) for consistent spacing. Whitespace and formatting normalized across Mountain (300+ files), Common, Echo, Grove, and Vine — standardizing blank lines, import organization, dev_log! alignment, and lock patterns. CI dependencies bumped: actions/checkout 6.0.2→6.0.3, protobumpjs 8.5.0→8.6.0. Mountain introduces domain dispatchers for 25+ IPC command categories (configuration, encryption, extensions, filesystem, git, keybindings, language features, lifecycle, logging, menubar, model, navigation, native host, notifications, output, process, progress, quick input, search, sky, storage, terminal, text files, themes, tree views, updates, URLs, working copy, workspace) plus UrlDispatcher stub.\n\nNo functional modifications or API breaking changes — purely mechanical formatting, README layout, dependency maintenance, and IPC infrastructure preparation.",
			"SHA": "afa20e75157acf69afe57055b025d7cdcd30c719"
		}
	],
